sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-20> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch11-20--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch11-20--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch11-20: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.67" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.673"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.66"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Mean curvature of a septal mesh, with the suture as the boundary condition, is a direct test of the soap-film claim, and public CT of chambered shells is sufficient to run it on a real sample. Coverage does not include every septal type, but the spherical, oblique and saddle cases are represented well enough to confirm or refute the geometry. Meshing and curvature are specialist but standard and can be done in weeks to a few months." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: From CT of nautiloid and ammonoid septa, estimate mean curvature given the suture as boundary, and compare spherical, ellipsoidal and saddle cases with the attachment Thompson describes. Near-zero mean curvature supports a minimal surface; systematic mean curvature, or a better fit by a non-minimal shell, refutes it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Downloadable CT is richer for Nautilus and a few ammonoids than for the full range of orthocones and suture types.", "A thin elastic membrane under pressure is minimal only under the isotropy and uniform-pressure assumptions." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch11-20--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch11-20--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch11-20--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch11-20 by Grok 4.7: 0.85" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.85"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch11-20--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-20> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch11-20--grok--operationalizability> .
